---
import Layout from '../../../../layouts/Layout.astro';import '../../../../styles/equipment.css';
const d='/equipment/15-02/',photo='https://downloads.microscope.healthcare.nikon.com/production/imager/productphotos/NIC-Systems/326272/Leuven-SMZ25_ec44f4f2c405bc67d4f5be9bb36fd56a.jpg',dims='https://downloads.microscope.healthcare.nikon.com/phase4/literature/Brochures/Japanese/StereoMicroscope_SMZ25-18_2CJ-MJHH-7.pdf#page=8';
---
<Layout pageTitle="Nikon SMZ25 static body and detached scale chart" description="Explore an inactive SMZ25 stereo microscope and verify scaling in a separate, fixed line drawing." wide={true}>
<article class="equipment" id="smz25"><nav class="eq-nav"><a href="/simulations/equipment/15-02/">← Equipment 15-02</a><a href="/simulations/equipment/">Register</a><a href="#sm-evidence">References and checks</a></nav>
<header class="eq-mast"><p class="eq-meta">15-02 / DORMANT MICROSCOPE · DETACHED SCALE CHART</p><h2>Double the display scale, keep the same distance</h2><p class="eq-lede">Inspect the sealed Nikon SMZ25 exterior. The separate, fixed chart demonstrates why a line can occupy more display pixels without becoming longer in the drawing’s units.</p></header>
<div class="sm-cols"><section><h3>Inert SMZ25 outer assembly</h3><canvas id="sm-model" aria-label="Orbitable Nikon SMZ25 outer geometry and physically separate scale chart stand"></canvas><p id="sm-viewstatus" role="status">Loading metric GLB…</p><button id="sm-front">Reset overview</button><button id="sm-side">Side view</button><button id="sm-board">Detached chart stand</button></section>
<section><h3>Offline 1 mm geometry chart</h3><label>Display scale <select id="sm-scale"><option value="1">1× display</option><option value="2">2× display</option></select></label><label>Reference marks <select id="sm-span"><option value="mm">Separate 1 mm marks</option><option value="zero">The same mark twice</option></select></label><button id="sm-toggle">Toggle chart scale</button>
<svg id="sm-diagram" viewBox="0 0 96 54" role="img" aria-label="Static line drawing with references shown at one or two times display scale">
<defs><pattern id="sm-paper" width="10" height="8" patternUnits="userSpaceOnUse"><path d="M10 0H0V8" fill="none" stroke="#3f6670" stroke-width=".35"/></pattern></defs><rect width="96" height="54" fill="#20343a"/>
<g id="sm-zoomGroup"><rect width="96" height="54" fill="url(#sm-paper)"/><path d="M23 30H73 M28 28V32 M38 27V33 M48 28V32 M58 27V33 M68 28V32" fill="none" stroke="#8bcfbc" stroke-width=".45"/><line id="sm-line" y1="23" y2="23" stroke="#ffca86" stroke-width=".7"/><circle id="sm-p0" cy="23" r="1.1" fill="#e9fff3"/><circle id="sm-p1" cy="23" r=".83" fill="#ffc981"/></g></svg>
<p id="sm-readout" role="status"></p><p id="sm-legend"></p><p>Chart pixels are logical drawing coordinates, not physical screen pixels. The 1 mm is an authored diagram length, not a microscope measurement or calibration.</p>
<button id="sm-export">Download chart summary</button><p><a href={d+'example-chart.json'}>Example at 2×</a>.</p></section></div>
<section id="sm-evidence"><h3>Selected configuration and checks</h3><div class="sm-cols"><figure><img src={d+'station.webp'} alt="Original inert Nikon body on white base, with opaque oculars and unrelated chart stand"/><figcaption>Original main-body and chart render. The <a href={photo}>Nikon-published KU Leuven SMZ25 photograph</a> informs the exterior shapes and dark/light surfaces. The pictured optional controller and auxiliary modules are not part of this reconstruction.</figcaption></figure>
<figure><img src={d+'side.webp'} alt="Original side render showing the fixed rear support, upper housing and static base"/><figcaption>Original side view modeled on <a href={dims}>Nikon catalogue 2CJ-MJHH-7, printed p. 14, motorized SMZ25 panel</a>. All mechanical details and individual accessory positions without marked dimensions are inferred; the exterior is inert.</figcaption></figure></div>
<table><thead><tr><th>Check</th><th>Expected</th><th>Actual / tolerance</th></tr></thead><tbody>
<tr><td>Primary assembly W × H × D</td><td>298 × 568 × 514 mm; indicated 25 mm ocular projection separate</td><td>Within 1 mm in exported GLB</td></tr><tr><td>Separate fiducials</td><td>20 chart px at 1×; 40 at 2×; 1 mm on both</td><td>Exact</td></tr><tr><td>Coincident point boundary</td><td>0 chart px at both scales</td><td>Exact; fixed chart remains unchanged</td></tr></tbody></table>
<p>The detached SVG applies the same display scale to both the pixel span and its legend. No optics, acquisition, focusing, specimen workflow, operative manipulation, biology or hardware calibration is modeled. The original register test is represented only as a geometry analogy.</p><p><a href={d+'build-model.py'}>Editable Blender source</a> · <a href={d+'smz25.glb'}>Metric GLB</a> · <a href={d+'chart.mjs'}>Fixed chart and report</a> · <a href={d+'vr.json'}>VR target bounds</a>. Headset use not verified.</p></section></article></Layout>
<script>import '../../../../lib/equipment/15-02/client.mjs';</script>
<style is:global>
#smz25 .sm-cols{display:grid;grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1.15fr) minmax(0,1fr);gap:1rem}#smz25 section{margin:1rem 0;padding:1rem;border:1px solid var(--border);min-width:0}
#smz25 :is(button,select){font:inherit;color:inherit;background:var(--panel);border:1px solid var(--border);padding:.4rem;margin:.2rem .25rem .2rem 0;max-width:100%}#smz25 button{cursor:pointer}#smz25 :is(button,select):focus-visible{outline:2px solid #b28d5e}
#sm-model{width:100%;height:354px;display:block;touch-action:none}#sm-diagram{width:min(100%,340px);display:block;margin:.45rem auto}#smz25 figure{margin:.5rem 0}#smz25 figure img{width:100%}
#smz25 table{width:100%;font-size:.94rem;border-collapse:collapse;text-align:left}#smz25 td,#smz25 th{border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);padding:.35rem}
@media(max-width:850px){#smz25 .sm-cols{grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1fr)}#sm-model{height:282px}}
</style>
